    "counseling_faq_GNN8AD": {
      "type": "counseling-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "faq_QMbJFd": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you accept insurance?",
            "answer": "<p>As a licensed Christian counseling practice, we provide faith-based pastoral counseling services that integrate Christian principles with holistic care. Because these services are pastoral in nature, we do not participate with or bill insurance companies directly. If you wish to seek possible reimbursement, we can provide a receipt for services rendered. You may submit this receipt to your insurance provider to determine whether your plan offers reimbursement for holistic, pastoral, or out-of-network counseling services. Please note that reimbursement is determined solely by your insurance provider and plan.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_derWe3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How is faith integrated into counseling?",
            "answer": "<p>Biblical wisdom is woven thoughtfully into each session. We integrate evidence-based therapeutic practices with scriptural truth. Prayer is always available but never forced. Our approach honors your faith journey at your pace.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_hWYYzz": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Is everything confidential?",
            "answer": "<p>Absolutely. Confidentiality is sacred to us. All sessions and records are kept strictly private in accordance with professional and legal ethical standards. Your trust and privacy are fully protected.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_3yEhQH": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you offer virtual appointments?",
            "answer": "<p>Yes. We offer secure, confidential telehealth sessions for clients who prefer remote counseling or have scheduling constraints. Virtual sessions provide the same level of care and attention as in-person visits.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_h9m4WU": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What should I expect at my first visit?",
            "answer": "<p>Your first session is a gentle, unhurried conversation. We will listen to your story, understand what brings you in, and begin shaping a personalized care plan. There is no pressure, only compassion and a safe space to begin.</p>"
          }
        },
        "faq_98NGqP": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "question": "Do you provide counseling to children?",
            "answer": "<p>We provide counseling for adults, including young adults ages (18+). Currently, we do not provide counseling for children or adolescents under the age of 18.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
